(1) Download the latest version of Raspbian - RASPBIAN JESSIE LITE

(2) Insert the SD card into the laptop/pc and run the image writer

(3) win32 disk imager - select device "E:" - select Raspbian image file "C:\pi" - "write"

(4) start pi login pi/raspberry

(5) in Setup Options --> Expand Filesystem - sudo raspi-config - df to see filesystem

(6) sudo raspi-config -> localisation -> locale -> en_US.UTF-8
(7) sudo raspi-config -> timezone -> America -> Central
(8) sudo dpkg-reconfigure keyboard-configuration -> Generic 105 key -> Other -> US (set AltGr to "Both Alt" and Compose to "Right Control")
(9) sudo apt-get install rpi-update  -  sudo rpi-update  -  sudo reboot
(10) sudo apt-get update --fix-missing  - sudo apt-get upgrade  -  sudo apt-get install oracle-java8-jdk postgresql iptables iptables-persistent
(10b) If wireless needed:
see: iwlist wlan0 scan
Change GB to US in /etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.conf
sudo bash -c "wpa_passphrase \"Gator Home\" \"LeeJe@nH0me9314\" >> /etc/wpa_supplicant/wpa_supplicant.conf"
sudo systemctl enable wpa_supplicant.service
sudo systemctl start wpa_supplicant.service
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
make sure changes are successful: ip addr show wlan0
(10c) for static host name, append the lines to dhcpcd.conf:

interface wlan0
static ip_address=192.168.1.6/24
static routers=192.168.1.1
static domain_name_servers=192.168.1.1
............
sudo reboot

(10d) if subversion is needed:
apt-get install subversion
extract latest tar archive from /mnt/pi/backups of svn
add "/usr/bin/svnserve -d -r /srv/svn" to /etc/rc.local
(10e) To enable ssh:
sudo raspi-config -> interfacing options->ssh

(11) postgresql files to edit: 
/etc/postgresql/9.4/main/pg_hba.conf
Second line: local	all	all	trust
Third line: host	all	all	samehost	md5
/etc/postgresql/9.4/main/postgresql.conf
max_connections=10
lc_messages='en_US.UTF-8'
lc_monetary='en_US.UTF-8'
lc_numeric='en_US.UTF-8'
lc_time='en_US.UTF-8'

(12) Recreate cluster with new localization:
if lc_messages lc_monetary, lc_numeric, and lc_time need to change:
sudo -u postgres pg_dropcluster --stop 9.4 main
sudo -u postgres pg_createcluster --start 9.4 main

if lc_messages, lc_monetary, lc_numeric, and lc_time are the same:
sudo -u postgres pg_ctlcluster 9.4 main reload
(13) for database/user setup
sudo -u postgres psql
\password
p$A2016aReSD

at command terminal sudo -u postgres createuser -d -P -h 127.0.0.1 -U postgres wildfly-admin
or
or psql terminal: CREATE USER "wildfly-admin";
or psql terminal: \password wildfly-admin

psql -U "wildfly-admin" -W -h 127.0.0.1 -d berrydb

CREATE DATABASE berrydb OWNER "wildfly-admin";


(14) sudo mkdir /srv/www; sudo chown www-data:www-data -R /srv/www
(15) mount -o uid=33,gid=33 /dev/sda1 /mnt
(16) Create wildfly-10.2.0.Final under /srv/www:
cd /srv/www
sudo -u www-data cp -R /mnt/pi/wildfly-10.2.0.Final-SNAPSHOT .
sudo umount /dev/sda1
(17) edit '/etc/profile' and after 'export PATH': 
export JAVA_HOME=/usr/lib/jvm/jdk-8-oracle-arm32-vfp-hflt;
export JBOSS_HOME=/srv/www/wildfly-10.2.0.Final-SNAPSHOT;

And then save the changes in terminal
. /etc/profile
(18) Update iptables
sudo iptables -N PREROUTING
sudo iptables -N POSTROUTING
For ethernet connections add: 

sudo iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -i eth0 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 80 -j DNAT --to-destination 192.168.1.3:8080
sudo iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -i eth0 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 443 -j DNAT --to-destination 192.168.1.3:8443

For wifi connections add:
sudo iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -i wlan0 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 80 -j DNAT --to-destination 192.168.1.3:8080
sudo iptables -t nat -A PREROUTING -i wlan0 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 443 -j DNAT --to-destination 

sudo iptables -t filter -A FORWARD -d 192.168.1.3/32 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 8080 -j ACCEPT
sudo iptables -t filter -A FORWARD -d 192.168.1.3/32 -p tcp -m tcp --dport 8443 -j ACCEPT
sudo bash -c "iptables-save -c > /etc/iptables/rules.v4"

(19) Go to the router WPS Wizard -> Advanced Setup -> Port Forwarding/Port Triggering
Add something like Wildfly-HTTPS
Add to the external port range: 443
Add the IP 192.168.1.3 then click Apply
Then go to the WPS Wizard -> Setup -> Internet Setup and view the IP.


